> - **Center:** A small, grassy clearing.
> - **Back of clearing:** A rough half‑circle of **druidic standing stones**, one of which is smoldering from a fire.
> - **Left side:** A couple of small trees, one actively burning at the base.
> - **Right side:** Brush and undergrowth, good for cover.
> - **Far side (opposite the party’s entry):** Humans partially circling the elf druid.
> 
> Let the players choose where they “pop out” from:
> - Behind a burning tree (left) – more fire risk, closer to one zealot.
> - Thicker brush (right) – more cover, great for a sneak attack.
> - Center path – direct and heroic, no cover.
> 
> ### B. Who’s Here? (Encounter Composition)
