> ## Finish Scene 5 – The Burning Grove: Running & Ending the Fight
> 
> ### Environmental bits (optional)
> 
> Use these only if you want more drama; ignore if you want a simpler fight.
> 
> - **Burning Tree Hazard**  
>   At initiative 20 each round:
>   - Embers fall from the burning tree.
>   - Any creature within 5 ft of the trunk: Dex save DC 11 or take 1d4 fire damage.
>   - After 3 rounds, the tree is close to collapse; if someone cuts it or you want big drama, it can fall:
>     - Dex save DC 12 or take 2d6 bludgeoning and be knocked prone; falling direction is your choice.
> 
> - **Sacred Stone**  
>   One standing stone has visible **druidic carvings** and faint green glow.
>   - If someone takes cover behind it, it grants **+2 AC** (half cover).
>   - If a zealot tries to topple it (STR check DC 13), the elf druid might shout “No!” and gain advantage on her next attack/spell against that zealot.
> 
> These details give Ekemon chances to use Titan-ish strength or clever positioning.
> 
> ### Ending Conditions
> 
> The fight ends when:
> 
> - All hostiles are defeated or routed. Likely:
>   - The **Purifier Captain** fights to 0 HP (you can decide if he dies outright or is stabilized for interrogation).
>   - The **Acolyte** might try to flee when alone or when the Captain falls.
>   - Any surviving **Zealots** may either surrender or flee into the woods.
> 
> If the kids like choices, you can explicitly ask:
> - “Do you let him run, or try to stop him?”  
> - “Do you keep this one alive to ask questions, or do you leave him?”  
> 
> It sets up later plot (the Inquisitor hearing of Ekemon, etc.).
