> ## Scene 6 – Immediate Aftermath: Meeting the Druid
> 
> **Purpose:** Cement the relationship, let everyone breathe, and seed the next leg of the Titan quest.
> 
> ### A. The Grove Cools Down
> 
> - The unnatural fire dies down once the acolyte is down / fleeing.
> - The elf druid uses a cantrip or small spell (Control Flames / Druidcraft / Create Water) to put out remaining embers.
> - Animals start to peek out again: birds in branches, a rabbit at the edge of the clearing.
> 
> If they restored a druid altar earlier on the road (Scene 1B), you can pay that off here:
> - The elf druid glances at them and says something like:
>   > “The grove knew you were coming. The Mother watches those who mend her shrines.”
> 
> ### B. Conversation & Thanks
> 
> Key beats to hit:
> 
> 1. **Introduction**
>    - She gives her name and simply: “I am a druid of the Greenwood, servant of the Fourfold Mother.”
>    - She thanks them sincerely:
>      > “If you hadn’t come when you did, I would be on my way to a human dungeon, or worse, this grove would be ash.”
> 
> 2. **Quick Lore Exchange**
>    - She explains what just happened, in very digestible terms:
>      - These were **Purifiers**, a harsh faction of the Human God church.
>      - They’ve been **hunting druids** and burning groves.
>      - They talk about a “storm‑idol” or “false heart of the world” ahead (the Titan Heartshard).
>    - She has heard rumors:
>      > “The sky above the old canyon temple has started to circle, even when the rest of the world is calm. Something ancient is waking there.”
> 
> 3. **Ekemon’s Titan Hook**
>    - She notices something about Ekemon:
>      - Maybe when she casts a small healing spell or touches his arm, she feels a deep vibration.
>    - You can give her a line like:
>      > “You carry a weight in your bones… old as mountains. You have walked close to Titans, haven’t you?”
>    - This is Ekemon’s chance to mention:
>      - The Titan Seed.
>      - The Titan Scale.
>      - Grima and the Sky‑Temple.
> 
> 4. **Shared Goal**
>    - Once she realizes they are heading to the same place:
>      > “Then our paths are bound together. The canyon temple is sacred to the Fourfold Mother, but something older stirs beneath it. If humans seize that power, it could break the land.”
>    - She offers to **guide them**:
>      - She knows a safer way through the Greenwood to reach the canyon rim.
>      - She knows some of the local politics and dangers.
> 
> ### C. Light Political Framing (kid-friendly)
> 
> Give Ekemon and Varkash a simple version:
> 
> - “Those humans follow a god they call the One Above. Many are kind, but some think all other gods—and all druids—are evil. Those ones are Purifiers.”
> - “We druids serve the Mother of Worlds and her four children—the gods of air, earth, fire, and water. We want balance, not war. But the Purifiers want to erase us.”
> 
> You can then let the kids react:
> - Do they sympathize?
> - Do they ask if the Human God is “real or fake”?
> - The druid might say something like:
>   > “He is real enough. But he is just one voice. The danger is when his followers try to silence all others.”
> 
> ### D. Short Rest & Minor Rewards
> 
> This is a perfect time for a **short rest**:
> 
> - Let them spend hit dice if you’re using that.
> - The druid can cast **Cure Wounds** on someone once as a thank-you.
> - Small tangible reward:
>   - She gifts Ekemon a **simple druidic charm** (a carved wooden token of Gaiaea or Aerian).
>     - Mechanical: 1/day, as a reaction, you can get +1d4 to a Nature or Survival check, or advantage on a single check related to tracking/finding the path.
>   - Or she shows them a **hidden shortcut** they’ll use next session (flavor only, but kids love being told “you found the secret path”).
> 
> ### E. Ending the Session
> 
> A clean stopping point:
> 
> - Camera pull-back moment:
>   - The three of them (Ekemon, Varkash, and the druid) stand in the half-burned grove as the smoke thins.
>   - Above the trees, very faint and distant, Ekemon hears a **single crack of thunder** from the direction of the canyon—no stormclouds in sight.
> 
> You can end with a teaser from the druid:
> 
> > “Tomorrow, I’ll lead you to the canyon’s edge. There you’ll see what your Titan heart is calling you toward… and you’ll see how many want to claim it before you do.”
> 
> Then: “We’ll pick up next time as you set out with your new ally toward the Canyon of Storms.”
